WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.260 --> 00:00:05.820
Speaker 1: So the question is, who is the
next big star of the Republican Party?

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:10.410
Well, there was a phenomenal piece written
this week by a good good friend of mine, Cliff

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:12.830
Schecter, writing for The Daily Beast.

00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:18.520
The piece is titled Dan Crenshaw is the Trumpist
of the wannabe new Trumps.

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:23.830
And in the piece, he talks about the fact
that sure, we've got other conservatives out

00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:26.930
there, kind of, you know, hinting at and testing
the waters.

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:30.210
You got your Nikki Haley, of course you got
you, Ted Cruz.

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:35.649
Maybe they're the ones to take up the mantle
of Trumpism here in the U.S.

00:00:35.649 --> 00:00:37.920
And then, of course, you've got the really
wackier ones.

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:43.300
You're Marjorie Taylor Greene's in your budgets,
in your Gates's.

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:46.660
But none of them, Cliff, points out.

00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:49.799
Have what Dan Crenshaw has.

00:00:49.799 --> 00:00:52.059
Dan Crenshaw.

00:00:52.059 --> 00:00:58.679
For the most part, is not as openly extreme
as some of those other individuals.

00:00:58.679 --> 00:01:05.370
He knows how to speak to an audience he effectively
has, as Cliff points out, what Trump had.

00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:07.440
That charisma.

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:11.120
Coupled with, of course, shamelessness and
cruelty.

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:18.190
But it's the charisma, it's his ability to
play to an audience, much like Donald Trump

00:01:18.190 --> 00:01:19.940
did.

00:01:19.940 --> 00:01:25.540
That is what makes Crenshaw so dangerous,
and of course, most likely the heir apparent

00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:29.110
to Donald Trump's entire political movement.

00:01:29.110 --> 00:01:35.530
You know, Crenshaw recently did an interview
where he called out the performance artists

00:01:35.530 --> 00:01:38.250
of the Republican Party.

00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:39.800
And he told us we know who they are.

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:40.870
He didn't want to name any names.

00:01:40.870 --> 00:01:43.060
He doesn't want to make any waves because
he's smart.

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:44.060
I'll give him that.

00:01:44.060 --> 00:01:45.060
He is smart.

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:49.090
He's good at what he does, but it's pretty
obvious that he is talking about your Marjorie

00:01:49.090 --> 00:01:50.421
Taylor Greene's in your law.

00:01:50.421 --> 00:01:54.980
And Bob, it's the people in Madison, Cawthorn,
the people who are out there just to get famous.

00:01:54.980 --> 00:01:56.930
They just want people to know their names.

00:01:56.930 --> 00:02:02.130
And as he pointed out correctly, by the way,
they're not doing anything legislatively,

00:02:02.130 --> 00:02:07.960
OK, they're not actually furthering the conservative
cause, as he says.

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:14.450
And his ability to call these people out and
seem as he's calling them out, like the rational

00:02:14.450 --> 00:02:20.709
choice, like the best alternative is what
does make him so incredibly dangerous as a

00:02:20.709 --> 00:02:24.099
potential candidate in the future.

00:02:24.099 --> 00:02:28.540
And then, of course, you have the performative
side.

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:31.450
Crenshaw has something the rest of them don't.

00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:36.049
He's got military credentials, and as Cliff
Schecter points out again.

00:02:36.049 --> 00:02:38.329
He's got the battle wound.

00:02:38.329 --> 00:02:42.770
He's got the eye patch, and I'm not saying
that to attack him, but that eyepatch is a

00:02:42.770 --> 00:02:49.620
constant reminder that he served, that he
went over there and fought the fight that

00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:55.599
these other conservatives only push from behind
their legislative desks.

00:02:55.599 --> 00:03:01.719
That makes a big difference with these Republican
candidates, somebody who can go out there

00:03:01.719 --> 00:03:05.879
and say, Oh, well, you say you support the
military, but I was actually in it.

00:03:05.879 --> 00:03:12.109
I fought it and I live with the ramifications
of it.

00:03:12.109 --> 00:03:17.560
He's got that tough guy persona that Donald
Trump could only pretend to have.

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:20.590
And of course, you do have the performance
artist in him, right?

00:03:20.590 --> 00:03:25.390
We've all seen the videos, the Crenshaw's
point out put out, excuse me himself, you

00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:30.959
know, rappelling down from the ceilings, acting
like some kind of Avenger slash secret agent

00:03:30.959 --> 00:03:31.959
guy.

00:03:31.959 --> 00:03:38.389
This big, tough bravado of only I can save
this.

00:03:38.389 --> 00:03:43.999
Which is kind of similar to what Donald Trump
actually said when he first ran for president.

00:03:43.999 --> 00:03:46.780
Only I can do this.

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:49.730
And that's what Crenshaw is putting out there.

00:03:49.730 --> 00:03:56.469
He appeals to the Trumpers, but he can act
sane enough because I do think to his credit,

00:03:56.469 --> 00:03:58.930
I think he is a sane person.

00:03:58.930 --> 00:04:02.540
But I think he knows when to turn on the crazy
and turn it off.

00:04:02.540 --> 00:04:05.840
And that's what separates him from the rest
of the pack.

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:09.860
That's what makes him different from a Marjorie
Taylor Greene.

00:04:09.860 --> 00:04:13.459
It's what makes him different from a Ted Cruz,
because Ted Cruz has gone full blown into

00:04:13.459 --> 00:04:16.769
all of this, he doesn't know who he is.

00:04:16.769 --> 00:04:22.290
But Crenshaw can turn it on and turn it off
like that.

00:04:22.290 --> 00:04:27.670
And as Cliff points out, that's something
that makes him incredibly valuable to the

00:04:27.670 --> 00:04:28.910
conservative movement.

00:04:28.910 --> 00:04:35.100
And, of course, makes him incredibly scary
as a potential Republican candidate in the

00:04:35.100 --> 00:04:36.760
future.

